WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.031 --> 00:00:00.864
(crowds cheering)

00:00:00.864 --> 00:00:03.590
- [Narrator] Soccer is the most
popular sport in the world.

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.840
And for soccer fans
there's a collectible item

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.910
that's taking their world by storm,

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.690
the Panini Soccer Sticker Album

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.563
that comes out every four years.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.010
We'll let this guy explain how it works.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.210
Because, well, he wrote an
entire book about stickers.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.720
- My name is Greg Lansdowne,

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.950
and I'm the author of “Stuck on You,”

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.728
the story of football stickers.

00:00:22.728 --> 00:00:27.728
(whistling and cheering)
(upbeat music)

00:00:28.848 --> 00:00:31.830
- [Narrator] OK, Greg, so,
what's this all about?

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.550
- Well it's a very simple concept.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:34.920
You start off with the album.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.170
And from there, you need to
collect packets of stickers.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.200
For the World Cup, there's
five stickers in every packet.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.970
In this particular World Cup album,

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.230
there's 682 spaces to fill.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.284
And the idea, or the name of the game,

00:00:47.284 --> 00:00:49.689
is to fill up the sticker album.

00:00:49.689 --> 00:00:52.290
Once you start to getting
doubles of stickers

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.020
that's when the real fun element comes in

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.595
and you start swapping with people.

00:00:55.595 --> 00:00:59.380
Panini's first album
Mexico '70 started off

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:00.880
with the album being distributed

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.920
in just a few European countries.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.850
That's now grown and you
can get Panini Stickers

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.280
in over 100 countries worldwide,

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.140
and that's growing
every single tournament.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.300
I'm sure they will leave no stone unturned

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.430
to make sure that you
get stickers in the hands

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:18.424
of everyone around the world, ultimately.

00:01:18.424 --> 00:01:20.470
- [Narrator] Who is the
biggest collector in the world?

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:22.780
- Well there is a gentleman in Italy,

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.380
the home of Panini Stickers.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.983
His name is Gianni Bellini,
and his sticker collection

00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:30.340
needs to be seen to be believed.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.765
- [Narrator] Introducing Gianni.

00:01:31.765 --> 00:01:34.682
(speaking Italian)

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.200
- [Narrator] Gianni lives
in a small town in Italy,

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.900
which happens to be only 20
miles from the Panini factory.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.817
(speaking Italian)

00:02:37.693 --> 00:02:38.690
- [Narrator] So, there you have it;

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.300
if you didn't know about soccer stickers,

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:43.603
now you can kick your own
collection into high gear.

